D('haulier',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The haulier collected the machinery and delivered it to the port.','货运承运人取走机器并将其运到港口。')],mistakes:[m('The haulier tried to mail the piano as a postcard.','The haulier transported the piano in a freight truck.','A large instrument must be carried as freight, not mailed as a postcard.')],quiz:[q('haulier',1,1,'In British English, a haulier is a person or firm that?','transports goods by road','sells hair products','repairs farm fences','haulier 是英式英语中的公路货运承运者。'),q('haulier',1,1,'A haulier’s invoice would most likely cover?','moving a machine to a warehouse','cutting a customer’s hair','teaching a music lesson','货运公司按运输服务收费。'),q('haulier',1,1,'Which term is closest to haulier?','freight carrier','hairdresser','harvester','freight carrier 指货运承运人。'),q('haulier',1,1,'The haulier arrived with a lorry to collect the shipment. The haulier?','was responsible for transporting it','had grown the shipment','was inspecting the weather','haulier 指负责运输货物的人或公司。')]});
D('haunch',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The deer lowered its head and sprang forward on its powerful haunches.','鹿低下头，用有力的臀腿部向前跃去。')],mistakes:[m('The chef sliced the haunch from the bird’s wing.','The chef sliced the haunch from the animal’s hindquarter.','haunch 指臀部及后腿上部，不是翅膀部位。')],quiz:[q('haunch',1,1,'An animal’s haunch is around its?','hip and upper hind leg','front paw','beak','haunch 指动物臀部和后腿上部。'),q('haunch',1,1,'A roast haunch of venison comes from?','the deer’s rear leg area','the deer’s antlers','the deer’s tongue','烤鹿臀腿肉取自后腿和臀部。'),q('haunch',1,1,'A dog crouched on its haunches is resting on?','its hindquarters','its front claws','its tail only','蹲坐姿势以臀腿部承重。'),q('haunch',1,1,'Which phrase is anatomically plausible?','muscular haunches','haunch feathers on a wing','a haunch of a tree','haunch 是动物身体部位，不是羽毛或树部位。')]});
D('haunt',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The old theater is said to be haunted by an actor who vanished there.','据说那座旧剧院里有一位曾在那里失踪的演员鬼魂出没。')],mistakes:[m('She was haunted by the memory but had forgotten it completely.','She was haunted by the memory and could not stop thinking about it.','被记忆困扰意味着无法摆脱，不是彻底忘记。')],quiz:[q('haunt',1,1,'A ghost is said to haunt the empty hotel. It?','appears there repeatedly','owns the hotel legally','repairs the elevators','鬼魂 haunt 某地指反复出没。'),q('haunt',2,2,'The village was a favorite haunt of painters. It was?','a place they often visited','a place they feared to name','a kind of paint','名词 haunt 可指某人常去的地方。'),q('haunt',3,3,'The accident continued to haunt him. He?','kept being troubled by its memory','forgot it the same day','celebrated it every year','比喻义是持续困扰或萦绕心头。'),q('haunt',4,4,'Which phrase means a place frequently visited?','an old haunt','a hunted memory','a ghosted calendar','old haunt 表示常去的老地方。')]});
D('haunted',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The children dared each other to enter the supposedly haunted mill.','孩子们互相激将，敢不敢进入据说闹鬼的磨坊。')],mistakes:[m('The haunted mansion had no ghosts, and its residents felt completely carefree.','The quiet mansion had no ghosts, and its residents never felt troubled by the past.','没有鬼魂且无人被过去困扰，不足以称 haunted。')],quiz:[q('haunted',1,1,'A haunted house is traditionally believed to contain?','ghosts','a hospital','a bakery','haunted 常描述据说有鬼魂出没的地方。'),q('haunted',2,2,'A haunted expression on her face suggests she looks?','troubled by painful memories','excited about a party','asleep','形容人的神情时可表示忧惧或被往事困扰。'),q('haunted',1,1,'Which sentence uses haunted literally?','The villagers say a ghost haunts the tower.','The villagers painted the tower blue.','The villagers harvested the tower.','字面义与鬼魂出没相关。'),q('haunted',2,2,'He had a haunted look after the disaster. He seemed?','deeply troubled','carefree','hungry','比喻义可形容神情受创、忧虑。')]});
D('haunting',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The haunting melody stayed with me long after the film ended.','电影结束很久后，那段萦绕心头的旋律仍留在我脑海里。')],mistakes:[m('The haunting tune disappeared from everyone’s memory within a second.','The forgettable tune disappeared from everyone’s memory within a second.','haunting 的旋律通常挥之不去，与瞬间被忘记相反。')],quiz:[q('haunting',1,1,'A haunting song is one that?','lingers in the mind and often feels moving','is too quiet to hear','has no melody','haunting 可指令人难忘、萦绕心头的。'),q('haunting',1,1,'The photograph’s haunting image left viewers uneasy. It was?','powerfully memorable and unsettling','plain and quickly forgotten','a photograph of a ghost only','haunting 可描述带来强烈情绪的画面。'),q('haunting',1,1,'Which collocation is natural?','a haunting melody','a hauntingly table','a haunt melody','haunting 可作形容词修饰 melody。'),q('haunting',1,1,'A haunting memory is one that?','keeps returning to someone’s thoughts','has never been experienced','is easy to discard','形容记忆时表示持续萦绕。')]});
D('have',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Our library may have two quiet rooms that visitors can reserve online.','我们的图书馆有两间可以在线预约的安静房间。')],mistakes:[m('They have breakfast yesterday before the exam.','They had breakfast yesterday before the exam.','过去时间 yesterday 要用 have 的过去式 had。')],quiz:[q('have',1,1,'This building has a rooftop garden. Here has means?','possesses or contains','eats quickly','must leave','have 可表示拥有或包含。'),q('have',2,2,'We had lunch near the station. Here had means?','ate','owned a station','were required','have 可表示吃一餐。'),q('have',4,4,'They had their windows repaired. What did they do?','arranged for someone to repair them','repaired them by eating lunch','refused to fix them','have something done 表示安排他人完成。'),q('have',5,5,'Which sentence uses have as a perfect auxiliary?','They have finished the report.','They have a report on the table.','They have breakfast at noon.','have finished 中 have 构成现在完成时。')]});
D('have fun',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Children have fun building cardboard forts in the garden.','孩子们在花园里搭纸板城堡，玩得很开心。')],mistakes:[m('We had fun at the picnic because everyone felt bored and miserable.','We had little fun at the picnic because everyone felt bored and miserable.','无聊难受和 had fun 的开心含义冲突，little 是最小改动。')],quiz:[q('have fun',1,1,'If the guests have fun at the reunion, they?','enjoy themselves','leave before it begins','argue throughout it','固定短语 have fun 表示玩得开心。'),q('have fun',1,1,'Choose the natural past-tense form.','They had fun at the fair.','They have funned at the fair.','They did fun at the fair.','have fun 的过去式是 had fun。'),q('have fun',1,1,'Which sentence gives friendly advice?','Have fun on your trip!','Have a funly on your trip!','Do fun to your trip!','Have fun 可用作祝愿。'),q('have fun',1,1,'The children had fun making kites. They found the activity?','enjoyable','dangerous by definition','impossible','have fun doing 表示做某事很开心。')]});
D('have on',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'What do you have on for the outdoor concert?','户外音乐会时你穿什么？')],mistakes:[m('She had on to her coat before leaving.','She had on her coat before leaving.','The clothing phrase have on takes the item directly, without to.')],quiz:[q('have on',1,1,'What did you have on at the ceremony? asks what you?','were wearing','owned in your house','had eaten','have on 可表示穿着。'),q('have on',1,1,'At the door, he had on a wet coat. He was?','wearing the coat','carrying the coat in a box','looking for a coat','have on 在描述衣着时等于 wear。'),q('have on',1,1,'Complete the question: What ___ she have on?','did','does to','was on','一般过去时疑问句用 did + have on。'),q('have on',1,1,'Which phrase asks about someone’s clothes?','What do you have on?','What have you eaten on?','Where do you have on?','该短语可询问某人穿了什么。')]});
D('have to',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Visitors have to sign in before entering the laboratory.','访客必须在进入实验室前登记。')],mistakes:[m('Yesterday she has to submit the form before noon.','Yesterday she had to submit the form before noon.','过去时间 yesterday 要用 had to 表示过去的义务。')],quiz:[q('have to',1,1,'If visitors have to sign in, signing in is?','required','forbidden','optional','have to 表示必须、不得不。'),q('have to',1,1,'Complete: We ___ leave now or we will miss the last bus.','have to','has to','having to','主语 we 后使用 have to。'),q('have to',1,1,'The road is closed, so drivers have to use the bridge. They?','must use the bridge','may never use any road','already crossed the bridge','语境说明绕行是必要要求。'),q('have to',1,1,'Which sentence refers to yesterday’s necessity?','I had to call the clinic yesterday.','I have to called the clinic yesterday.','I has to call yesterday.','过去时形式是 had to。')]});
D('haven',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'After weeks at sea, the sheltered bay offered the crew a safe haven.','在海上航行数周后，这处避风湾为船员提供了安全港湾。')],mistakes:[m('The refugees found a haven, a place where they were hunted and unsafe.','The refugees found a refuge, a place where they were protected and safe.','haven 指避难所或安全处，受追捕的不安全地点不符合词义。')],quiz:[q('haven',1,1,'A safe haven for boats is?','a protected place where they can shelter','a cliff with no landing','a fishing net','haven 可指船只停泊避风的安全港湾。'),q('haven',2,2,'The library became a haven from the noise. It was?','a peaceful refuge','the loudest room','a place to buy engines','引申义指能躲避压力或危险的安宁处。'),q('haven',3,3,'A tax haven is a place known for?','favorable tax arrangements','heavy snowfall','shipbuilding only','tax haven 是税务安排有利的地区。'),q('haven',1,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a haven for endangered birds','a haven of loud traffic','a haven at the storm’s center','haven 常与 for 连用说明受庇护对象。')]});
D('having',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Having checked the figures twice, Jo sent the budget to the director.','乔把数字核对两遍后，将预算发给了主管。')],mistakes:[m('Having finish the audit, Jo filed the report.','Having finished the audit, Jo filed the report.','having 后接过去分词构成完成分词结构，finish 应为 finished。')],quiz:[q('having',1,1,'Having finished dinner, they went for a walk. Which happened first?','They finished dinner.','They went for a walk.','They bought dinner tomorrow.','Having finished 表示晚饭先完成。'),q('having',1,1,'Choose the correct form: ___ read the instructions, Kim began assembly.','Having','Have','Has','Having + 过去分词构成完成分词短语。'),q('having',1,1,'In “having a difficult day,” having is part of?','the verb phrase have a day','a plural noun','a past-tense modal','having 可是动词 have 的 -ing 形式。'),q('having',1,1,'Which sentence is grammatically correct?','Having locked the door, she left.','Having lock the door, she left.','Having locks the door, she left.','完成分词结构中 having 后用过去分词 locked。')]});
D('havoc',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'A burst pipe caused havoc in the basement, ruining boxes and electrical equipment.','水管爆裂在地下室造成严重破坏，毁坏了箱子和电气设备。')],mistakes:[m('The storm wreaked havoc by leaving every house and road completely undamaged.','The storm caused no damage, leaving every house and road undamaged.','An event that causes no damage has not wreaked havoc.')],quiz:[q('havoc',1,1,'The flood wreaked havoc on the town. It?','caused widespread damage and disorder','made every street cleaner','built new houses','havoc 表示严重破坏和混乱。'),q('havoc',2,2,'A computer virus can play havoc with files by?','corrupting or disrupting them','printing them neatly','watering them','play havoc with 表示严重扰乱或损坏。'),q('havoc',1,1,'Which verb commonly pairs with havoc?','wreak','whisper','bake','固定表达 wreak havoc 表示造成严重破坏。'),q('havoc',1,1,'After the outage, the schedule was in havoc. More idiomatically it was?','in chaos','in a harbor','in harmony','havoc 相关常见表达是 chaos/disorder。')]});
